# C19 - failover provider base URLs

Status: complete (commit aca04ea on khamis1992/cc-c19)

## What changed
`src/config.ts` - the hard-coded `failover.providers` defaults were guessed and
never verified, so failover calls went to hosts that do not serve the documented
API. Each entry is now backed by evidence:

| provider | before | after | evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| longcat | `https://api.longcat.ai/v1` | `https://api.longcat.chat/openai/v1` | LongCat API Platform Quick Start: OpenAI-format endpoint `https://api.longcat.chat/openai/v1/chat/completions`, model `LongCat-2.5-Preview` |
| opencode-go | `https://api.opencode.ai/v1` | `https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1` | OpenCode "Go" docs, Endpoints table: `https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1/chat/completions` (the old host returns 404 for `/v1/models`) |
| freellmapi | `https://api.freellmapi.com/v1` | `http://127.0.0.1:31415/v1` | freellmapi is a self-hosted router with no documented public endpoint; `docs/agents-state.json` records `freellmapi/auto unreachable: localhost:31415 down`. Left `enabled: true` as found and marked `// TODO(C19): unverified endpoint` |
| ornith | `https://api.ornith.ai/v1` | `http://127.0.0.1:11434` (kind `ollama`, model `ornith-1.5:9b`) | `docs/handoff/oc-local.json` and `docs/handoff/watchdog.ps1` both define it as a local Ollama model; `api.ornith.ai` is not a documented service |

`DEFAULTS` is now exported so the defaults can be pinned by tests.

## Test added
`src/__tests__/configFailover.test.ts` (node:test) asserts:
1. `longcat.baseUrl === "https://api.longcat.chat/openai/v1"`;
2. every *enabled* provider `baseUrl` parses as an absolute http(s) URL with no
   trailing slash (a trailing slash yields `//chat/completions`);
3. no provider embeds a key value - `apiKeyEnv` is empty or an env-var name, and
   no other string field is a high-entropy token.

No secrets are present in the committed code.

## Gates
- `npx tsc --noEmit` - pass
- `npm run build:server` - pass (dist/server.cjs 19.3mb)
- `node --import tsx --test src/__tests__/configFailover.test.ts` - pass (3/3)
- touched-area suites (`codingRouter`, `failover`, `modelAudit`, `codingBenchmark`,
  `codingRouting`) - 57 pass, 0 fail

## Not done / follow-up
`freellmapi` has no documented public endpoint, so its URL is unverified by
design (TODO(C19)); the entry is otherwise unchanged. The task's "round-robin"
naming refers to the existing failover chain walk in `src/llm/failover.ts`,
which already implements ordered failover plus per-provider cooldown; no
behaviour change was needed there.
